-- title:
--   Integral independent family on Γ₁(M) of dimension-formula size
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive natural number with $M \ge 5$ and let $k$ be a natural number with $k \ge 3$. Then there exist a natural number $d$, a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to M_k(\Gamma_1(M))$ of modular forms of weight $k$ (viewed as an integer) for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$, and a family $pg : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ of integral power series such that: (i) for every $i$, the predicate `IsIntegralQExp` holds for $g i$ and $pg i$, that is, the image of $pg\,i$ under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $g\,i$ taken with respect to width $1$; (ii) the family $g$ is linearly independent over $\mathbb{C}$; and (iii) the numerical inequality
--   $$(k-1)\,[\,\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\cdot\langle -1\rangle\,] + 6\,\#\bigl(\Gamma_1(M) \backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) / \langle T, -1\rangle\bigr) \le 12\,d$$
--   holds, where the index is that of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ and $-1$, and the second term counts the double cosets of the subset $\Gamma_1(M)$ and of the subgroup generated by the translation matrix $T$ together with $-1$ (the cusp count), all arithmetic being in $\mathbb{N}$.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma_1(M)$ form of the assertion that the space of weight-$k$ forms contains a $\mathbb{C}$-linearly independent family of forms with integral $q$-expansions whose size is at least the Riemann–Roch dimension bound $\bigl((k-1)n + 6c\bigr)/12$, with $n$ the index of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$ and $c$ the cusp count. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_intSeriesC_gamma1_of_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_intSeriesC_gamma1_of_le) as the source of integral families to which reduction arguments are applied.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_complex_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CongruenceSubgroup
open ModularCurve
open scoped MatrixGroups ModularForm

theorem ModularCurve.exists_isIntegralQExp_linearIndependent_complex_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card
    (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (hM : 5 ≤ M) (k : ℕ) (hk : 3 ≤ k) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (g : Fin d → ModularForm (Gamma1 M) (k : ℤ)) (pg : Fin d → PowerSeries ℤ),
      (∀ i, IsIntegralQExp (g i) (pg i)) ∧ LinearIndependent ℂ g ∧
      (k - 1) * (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1 : SL(2, ℤ))).index +
          6 * Nat.card (DoubleCoset.Quotient (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M : Set SL(2, ℤ))
            ((Subgroup.zpowers ModularGroup.T ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1) : Subgroup SL(2, ℤ)) : Set SL(2, ℤ)))
        ≤ 12 * d := by sorry
